{"name":"Midnight Badger","hex":"#585960","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"midnight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The middle of the night: the sixth temporal hour, equidistant between sunset and sunrise.","Twelve o'clock at night exactly."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Utterly dark or black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midnight"},{"term":"badger","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of species of the genera Meles, Arctonyx, Mellivora or Taxidea, of mammals.","A native or resident of the American state, Wisconsin."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pester; to annoy persistently; to press."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/badger"}],"entries":[{"title":"Midnight","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight is the transition time from one day to the next – the moment when the date changes, on the local official clock time for any particular jurisdiction. By clock time, midnight is the opposite of noon, differing from it by 12 hours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight","wikidata":"Q36402"},{"title":"Badger","blocks":[{"text":"Badgers are medium-sized short-legged omnivores in the superfamily Musteloidea. Badgers are a polyphyletic rather than a natural taxonomic grouping, being united by their squat bodies and adaptions for fossorial activity rather than by their ancestral relationships: Musteloidea contains several families, only two of which include badgers; moreover, both of these families also include various other animals that are not badgers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/European_badger_%28Meles_meles_taxus%29_Drenthe.jpg/330px-European_badger_%28Meles_meles_taxus%29_Drenthe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badger","wikidata":"Q638105"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photograph of the moon taken at midnight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidnight_Mist.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Badger_laying_on_ground._-_DPLA_-_0335977b4d1504edc799834081ca4fd5.jpg/500px-Badger_laying_on_ground._-_DPLA_-_0335977b4d1504edc799834081ca4fd5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Badger_laying_on_ground._-_DPLA_-_0335977b4d1504edc799834081ca4fd5.jpg/500px-Badger_laying_on_ground._-_DPLA_-_0335977b4d1504edc799834081ca4fd5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An American badger","link":"http